.TH SHIWAKE 1 "2026-10-27" "shiwake" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
shiwake \- sort the files of a folder into A to Z subfolders by first letter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B shiwake
.br
.B shiwake
.RI [ options ] " " [ folder ]
.br
.B shiwake doctor
.br
.B shiwake version
.br
.B shiwake help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B shiwake
moves every file at the top of a folder into a subfolder named for the first
letter of the file's name, creating each subfolder the first time it is
needed. Letters go to
.B A
through
.BR Z ,
whatever their case. Any other first character, such as a digit, a symbol or
an accented letter, sends the file to
.BR # .
.PP
Symbolic links move like files and are never followed. Subfolders, hidden
files and special files stay where they are. A file is never moved over one of
the same name: it stays, and shiwake prints a warning naming it. When a file
or a link already stands where a letter folder belongs, the files for that
letter stay where they are.
.PP
Before moving anything, shiwake prints the folder and how many files go into
how many subfolders. Without a folder on a terminal it asks for one, offering
the current folder; outside a terminal it sorts the current folder.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B doctor
List the tools shiwake needs, with the flavor and version of each. Exits
non-zero only when one is missing.
.TP
.B version
Print the version and the platform.
.TP
.B help
Print the usage page.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
List every move and change nothing.
.PP
.B \-\-
ends the options. A folder named help, doctor or version is sorted by giving
its path, such as
.IR ./help .
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when every file that could move did, including runs where some files stayed
because their folder already holds a file of the same name. 1 when a file
could not be moved, a letter folder could not be made, or the arguments are
wrong.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B shiwake ~/Downloads
Sort the Downloads folder.
.TP
.B shiwake \-\-dry\-run .
Show what sorting the current folder would do.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mv (1),
.BR mkdir (1)
